56.6929133858267775 532.9136220472440755 Td
(What bounce is: 'Bouncing' refers to the mechanical vibrations in a switch's contacts as they close or open,) Tj
T* (which generate a series of erratic, rapid voltage spikes instead of a clean transition.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (How your solution fixes it: The solution fixes this by introducing a time threshold \(debounce delay of 50ms\)) Tj
T* (using the time.monotonic\(\) function. Once a state change is detected, the algorithm waits for the physical) Tj
T* (contacts to settle. It only registers the input as valid if the signal remains stable after this time period.) Tj
